<title>UK: Murray Income NAV rises in first half.</title>
<headline>Murray Income NAV rises in first half.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		37.92		  vs 40.63</p>
<p> Pretax		     33.83		  vs 36.14</p>
<p> Revenue attributable   32.48		  vs 34.78</p>
<p> Net asset value(pence) 409.5		  vs 376.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Murray Income Trust Plc forecast a final year dividend of 5.35p making a total of 13.9p per share. For the year to June 1998, it forecast an interim dividend of 9.0p, payable in three instalments.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
